{
  "source": "Ingredients: hollow-orbit js/game/items.js, Rust's where it has the item (spears, bow, arrows). Times are ours, between hollow-orbit's and Rust's. G4: gunpowder (30 charcoal and 20 sulphur make 10), pistol and rifle rounds (10 metal fragments and 5 gunpowder make 4 and 3, at workbench 1 and 2) and the rifle's tier (workbench 3) are hollow-orbit's and Rust's; the variants, attachments and the metal mask are ours. Building items (G3): hollow-orbit's plan, hammer, claim device (its tool cupboard), wooden and sheet metal doors and code lock; Rust's key lock, double and garage doors and workbench levels; G5: Rust's raiding recipes and workbench levels (explosives 50 gunpowder, 3 low-grade fuel, 10 sulphur and 10 metal fragments at workbench 2; the timed charge 20 explosives at 3; the satchel-like bag charge four grenades at 1; the grenade 60 gunpowder and 20 metal fragments; rockets 10 explosives and 150 gunpowder, the high-velocity one 100 gunpowder, the incendiary one (IW4) 150 gunpowder and 75 low-grade fuel; explosive rounds 20 gunpowder and 10 sulphur for two, at 3), so a timed charge costs 2,200 sulphur, a rocket 1,400, a bag charge 480 and an explosive round 25, as in Rust. Lamp oil stands in for low-grade fuel, fibre for cloth and the stash. G6 (ours): the vehicle workbench at workbench 2, and the Tin Finch built at a vehicle workbench (its 'station'): mostly metal, with lamp oil for its first tank. G7 (world.json): salvage pays for workbenches as in Rust (50, 500, 1,250), and the level 2 and 3 workbenches also need three torn or sealed schematics (Rust's blueprint fragments); higher tiers need components as in Rust: the pistol a receiver and a pipe, the rifle a rifle frame and four springs, sights tech scrap, the silencer a pipe, the garage and armoured doors gears, rockets and the launcher pipes, the timed charge tech scrap, the bag charge rope, the bed a sewing kit; rope, cloth and the sewing kit are made of fibre (our cloth), the research table of metal fragments and salvage (Rust's). Which recipes a player knows: those in no tech tree from the start, the rest once learnt (world.json). G7 animals: Rust's low-grade fuel recipe (3 animal fat and 1 cloth make 4 in 5 s) as a second way to make lamp oil, with its own key and id (220), beside the charcoal recipe; Rust's bone knife (30 bone fragments) and a bone club (20); all three in no tech tree, so known from the start (as in Rust).",
  "workbenchSpeed": {
    "note": "GROUND_SYSTEMS.md §7: a workbench above the level a recipe needs crafts it faster (Rust's: one level above, half the time; two or more, a quarter). Each job's time is fixed when it starts, by the best workbench in reach then; the list's place is the levels above (the last holds for more). A recipe made at a station of its own (a ship at the vehicle workbench) takes its own time.",
    "byLevelsAbove": [1, 0.5, 0.25]
  },
